# Line endings are pinned deliberately, not for tidiness.
#
# The modularization of WindowTweaks.ahk is verified by a "motion proof": the
# resolved #Include stream is sorted and hashed, and a pure code-motion commit
# must not change that hash (scripts\Check-Split.ps1). With core.autocrlf=true
# and no rules here, files round-trip between LF and CRLF depending on which
# tool last wrote them - src\RenderCore.ahk was already LF in the working tree
# while every other .ahk was CRLF - and the hash then differs for reasons that
# have nothing to do with the code. Pinning makes checkout deterministic.
#
# Everything here is a Windows-only project (AutoHotkey v2, PowerShell, WinForms
# setup), so CRLF is the native choice and nothing reads these on a Unix host.

*.ahk   text eol=crlf
*.ps1   text eol=crlf
*.cs    text eol=crlf
*.md    text eol=crlf
*.json  text eol=crlf
*.rsp   text eol=crlf

# Binary - never touch, never diff.
*.ico   binary
*.exe   binary
*.png   binary
